            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0138" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/871: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hare</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-15T20:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. Your 102, June 12, 6 p.m. Americans may travel on neutral ships proceeding
                    out of Mediterranean through combat areas but they do so at their own risk and
                    contrary to Department’s advice.</p>
                <p>Blanket authority hereby given you to validate passports for one journey through
                    combat area on neutral ships for Americans choosing so to proceed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
